<h1>David Sheppard</h1>
<p>Illinois House, 36th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Republican.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.shep4staterep.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (shep4staterep.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>His campaign commitments are supporting law enforcement and cracking down on crime, stopping tax hikes, rolling back automatic gas tax increases and capping property taxes, and focusing schools on academics, parental involvement and support for children with special needs.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Spent 28 years in law enforcement in corrections, patrol and investigations, rising to chief of the Robbins Police Department, and serves on the Evergreen Park School District 124 board.</p>
